{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1379337-homebrew-wyrd-beats","id":1379337,"title":"[Homebrew] Wyrd Beats","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-07T15:33:52-07:00","id":1379337,"title":"[Homebrew] Wyrd Beats","content":"EDIT: This house rule has been updated after my increased familiarity with Beats in Changeling 2ed. In this revision, the following circumstances are simply additional sources of Beats.<br /> <br /> 1) Avoid directly confronting a Huntsman in a way that causes meaningful complications and hardships. Gain a full Experience if you manage to return the Huntsman's Heart.<br /> <br /> 2) Successfully confront your Keeper face-to-face in a manner that reaffirms your freedom and identity. This gives a full Experience if you manage to do it inside the Hedge or Dreams.<br /> <br /> 3) Get significantly lost while travelling through the Hedge or Dreams, with all that entails.<br /> <br /> 4) Have a full scene of meaningful interaction with your Fetch, be it positive or negative. If you successfully merge with your Fetch [Autumn Nightmares Page 106], you may develop a custom Persistent Condition that gives Beats in addition to the usual benefits of Fetch-Merging.<br /> <br /> 5) Each Motley possesses a shared and additional Long Term Aspiration, which is to be phrased as a recurring pattern, theme or motif of fairy tales, urban legends, or equivalent dramaturgical medium. The Wyrd arranges events for their lives to manifest narratives with symbolically resonant conflicts that would generate Beats. Whenever a PC gets a Beat from this additional Long Term Aspiration, they also get 1 Glamour. This Long Term Aspiration may be changed once per Story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com